# NOT blocked on purpose: login.php, logout.php, verify.php, account.php,
# dashboard.php, checkout.php and pantry-scan.php. These pages carry a noindex meta tag,
# and a URL blocked here is never fetched — so the noindex is never seen and
# the page stays in the index as "Indexed, though blocked by robots.txt".
# Letting Google crawl them is what gets them OUT. Only endpoints with real
# side effects belong below.

# CRAWL TRAPS — infinite URL space and action endpoints.
# build-day.php, mix.php and explore.php take a random ?seed=, so every value is a
# distinct URL and the space never ends. Googlebot had already spent 46 crawls on
# 46 different build-day seeds — none of which can ever be a landing page — while
# the recipe pages it should be indexing waited their turn. The rest below are
# buttons, not pages: they act and redirect.
